# A homolog (staging) environment, proxied to its own VM on the LAN. See
# docs/adr/0035-homolog-environment.md.
#
# This file is a template. On the production server, copy it to
# caddy/sites/homolog.caddy, put in the real hostname and the homolog VM's
# address, and restart caddy:
#
#   docker compose restart caddy
#
# caddy/sites/ is gitignored and deploy.sh never transfers or deletes it, so the
# site stays on this server and out of the public repository.

zoia-homolog.example.com {
	import zoia_app

	# Plain HTTP across the LAN to the homolog VM's app. The public leg is TLS,
	# terminated here like every other site.
	reverse_proxy <homolog-vm-ip>:3000
}
